CLASS:: MP2Pack
SUMMARY:: Write compressed fields as a valid MPEG stream
CATEGORIES:: UGens>MPEG Audio
RELATED:: Guides/MPEGAudio, Classes/MP2Unpack, Classes/MP2Decode

DESCRIPTION::
Fit each edited frame into a legal bit budget. A file path is optional. Live byte and field outputs are available with the recorder stopped.

CLASSMETHODS::
METHOD:: ar
A finished take is moved into place when run falls. A change of effective rate or channel count finishes an open take.

ARGUMENT:: fields
An MPEGFrame for the same layer. Encoders, readers and the MPEGFrame constructors all supply this type.

ARGUMENT:: path
Full path on the server, supplied as a String when building the SynthDef.

ARGUMENT:: run
A rising edge starts a take or starts reading at the beginning. A falling edge finishes the take or stops reading.

ARGUMENT:: bitrate
Requested kb/s. A control or audio-rate signal can change it at a frame boundary. The object selects the nearest legal rate.

ARGUMENT:: freeze
A gate of 1 holds the last frame, including its level. Set to 0 to follow live data.

ARGUMENT:: holds
Per-band gates. A single value broadcasts, 32 values address a bank, and 64 values address left and right independently.

ARGUMENT:: holdMode
Use a symbol, code::\coeff:: or code::\level::, or a signal carrying 0 or 1. Level mode preserves the held band level.

ARGUMENT:: downsample
Native clock divisor from 1 to 6. A reader samples this at start. Connected field streams preserve the original codec clock.

ARGUMENT:: normalized
Set to 1 for bipolar words in the range −1 to 1. The default expects signed codec integers.

ARGUMENT:: monitor
Set to 1 to synthesize the samples represented by the packed bytes. Read them from the returned frame’s code::audio:: member.

RETURNS:: An MPEGFrame with the edited fields before fitting, packed byte lanes, optional audio monitor and status.

EXAMPLES::
code::
{ var f = MPEGFrame.mp2(SinOsc.ar([2,3,5])*12); var p = MP2Pack.ar(f, bitrate:96, monitor:1); Limiter.ar(p.audio,0.15) ! 2 }.play;
::
